From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bommu Krishnaiah <krishnaiah.bommu@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:37:22 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/xe/eudebug: Do not warn when debugging is unsupported

XE_EUDEBUG_NOT_SUPPORTED is a valid zero-valued state. Initialization
leaves the device in this state for SR-IOV VFs and when EUdebug setup
fails. Ordinary pagefault handling also checks whether EUdebug is
enabled, so warning on a zero state taints the kernel even without a
debugger session.

Return false for unsupported devices without warning. Initialization
failures retain their existing diagnostic messages.

Signed-off-by: Bommu Krishnaiah <krishnaiah.bommu@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/prelim/xe_eudebug.c
@@ -2429,9 +2429,6 @@ int prelim_xe_eudebug_connect_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
 
 bool prelim_xe_eudebug_is_enabled(struct xe_device *xe)
 {
-	if (XE_WARN_ON(!xe->eudebug.state))
-		return false;
-
 	return xe->eudebug.state == XE_EUDEBUG_ENABLED;
 }
 
